  "prefLabel": "Cub 307.02 Development Other Than Condominiums",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Cub 307.02 Development Other Than Condominiums.\n\n(a) In the case of a development, other than condominiums, any land in the development area undergoing physical changes as referenced in Cub 301.02, including land identified in the development plan required to satisfy the density, setback, or other condition, that requires that land to remain undeveloped as part of the plan approval shall be removed from current use pursuant to RSA 79-A:7, I.\n\n(b) Any lot or site, or combination of adjacent lots or sites shown thereon, which are under identical ownership shall remain in current use until such time as there is no longer 10 qualifying acres of developable land, as shown on the approved development plan.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 and Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Cub 300) #12857-B, eff 8-23-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/cub100-300.html"
